  {:id :independent-binding-and-record-matrix
   :finding "Each artifact binding field is removed and substituted with a generic string, but realistic same-shaped pins, expected-record substitutions, expected extras, schema/format substitutions and coherent changes of both sides are not covered."
   :fix "For all 12 fields test correctly typed alternate values independently in artifact and expected records, missing/extra/wrong-type keys on both, malformed and uppercase revision hashes, and constants versus externally provisioned revision values. Test separately changed closed top-level fields/counts/digests. If both sides share a different well-formed external revision the pure API may accept it: do not assert it authenticates the caller; static fixed constants must still reject substitutions. Assert nil/unavailable expected binding denies render and validate without fallback."}
  {:id :strict-utf8-and-octet-isolation
   :finding "Invalid vectors are tested only with stale metadata, so a count/hash check could mask a lax decoder; raw vector ceiling checks use invalid repeated ASCII unrelated to a valid artifact."
   :fix "For both fields cover unsigned vector domain and strict malformed UTF-8 classes, including overlong, truncated, continuation, surrogate and above-U+10FFFF. Give each malformed UTF-8 vector matching count and independently computed raw-octet digest where feasible, so it cannot be dismissed as stale metadata; do not obtain the hash through a replacement decoder. Check accepted Unicode/non-BMP bytes, re-encoding and independently fixed SHA-256 goldens; assert sanitized failures and invalid host surrogates/NUL without input echo. Separate over-bound vector tests from grammar checks."
   }
  {:id :reachable-inclusive-boundaries
   :finding "32767/32768 input positives exist, but all raw 65535/65536 vectors are invalid and no escaped boundary artifact is accepted."
   :proof "For any canonical shared value with escaped-byte length E, payload length is 20+E and descriptor length 45+E; thus descriptor is always 25 bytes larger. With both ceilings 65536, valid payload is at most 65511; payload 65535/65536 cannot occur in a valid artifact. This follows from the fixed byte goldens (26 and 51 for six-byte lambda) and shared escaping, not from a runtime probe."
   :fix "Exercise valid rendered and independently validated descriptor lengths 65535 and 65536 using 10915 U+0001 characters (6 escaped bytes each), respectively plus zero or one ASCII character; assert exact counts, raw octets/digests and paired payload lengths 65510 and 65511. Add 65537 descriptor via two ASCII characters and require render denial; separately require rejection for over-limit raw vectors. Check value lengths 32767/32768 accepted and 32769 rejected, including multibyte byte-count examples and escaped expansion; do not demand impossible valid 65536 payload. Use independent expected construction and count/digest oracles."}
